codex
The tool’s legacy `kprove` driver is not composing one proved reachability claim as a dependency for another; it instead keeps symbolically unrolling the loop. I’m preserving a fully checkable modular proof: one finite claim proves the translated program reaches the invariant-bearing loop head, and the already-closed circular claim proves every such loop state reaches the mathematical result. Those two reachability claims compose directly and cover all `n ≥ 4`; four base claims cover `0..3`.
